import site/games/farm/simulation.dl

set roles to the initial website farm roles
require condition (the length of roles = 1) reporting "The Farm gained an unsolicited example role."
set original to the item at 0 in roles
require condition ((original's id = "lumberjack") and ((original's name = "Lumberjack") and (original's prepared = false))) reporting "The initial Farm role changed."
require condition (original's source starts with "# Bring logs back, keeping one hand for the axe.") reporting "The Lumberjack example lost its explanation."
set original's source to original's source + "\n# An owned draft 🌽"
set original's applied to "loop forever:\n    turn right"
free website farm plan the address of (original's program)
set original's program to the website farm plan from (the string form of "LOOP|-1\nDO|1|3|-1|-2|\nEND") dropping 2 source lines
set original's prepared to true
set original's generation to 7
set copy to a copy of website farm role original identified by (the string form of "custom-a") among roles
set another to a copy of website farm role original identified by (the string form of "custom-b") among roles
require condition ((copy's name = "Lumberjack copy") and (another's name = "Lumberjack copy 2")) reporting "Copied Farm roles have duplicate names."
require condition ((copy's generation = 0) and (copy's applied = original's applied)) reporting "A copied role retained its request generation or lost its applied code."
set changed to the item at 1 in (copy's program's code)
set changed's argument to 2
replace item at index 1 in (copy's program's code) with changed
set original's source to ""
require condition ((the item at 1 in (original's program's code))'s argument = 3) reporting "Editing a copied plan changed its source role."
require condition (copy's source ends with "# An owned draft 🌽") reporting "Editing a source role invalidated its copied draft."
set world to the initial website farm world
set worker to the item at 0 in (world's workers)
assign website farm role original to worker
advance the website farm world world using roles roles with workers running true
require condition (worker's direction = 1) reporting "The original worker did not turn right."
assign website farm role copy to worker
advance the website farm world world using roles roles with workers running true
require condition (worker's direction = 0) reporting "The copied worker did not use its own modified plan."
clear the website farm role of worker
require condition ((worker's role is empty) and ((worker's routine's position = 0) and (worker's subject's kind = 0))) reporting "Removing a role kept its execution state."
free website farm world world
free website farm roles roles
print line "Farm role copies keep independent drafts, programs and names, and workers use the assigned plan."
